
# Hiring Manager / Behavioral Interview Questions

## A. Ownership & Responsibility (5)

1. What has been your biggest contribution to your current project?
2. Tell me about something you improved on your own without being asked.
3. Tell me about a mistake you made in production and what you learned from it.
4. Have you ever missed a task or deadline? What happened?
5. If you believe a requirement for the task you were given is incorrect, what would you do?

## B. Pressure & Deadlines (5)

6. Tell me about a time you worked under a tight deadline. How did you manage it?
7. If you receive multiple tasks at the same time, how do you decide which one to prioritize?
8. If you find a critical bug one day before a release, what would you do?
9. What would you do if you were assigned a task that you did not know how to do?
10. Have you ever worked under a lot of stress? How did you handle it?

## C. Team & Conflict (5)

11. Tell me about a disagreement you had with a teammate. How did you handle it?
12. What would you do if a senior rejected your approach?
13. How would you deal with a teammate who does not cooperate or help with the work?
14. Have you ever helped or mentored a junior or a new team member?
15. What would you do if you and your manager had different opinions about something?

## D. Learning & Growth (5)

16. What new things have you learned in the past year?
17. How do you learn a new technology? Give me an example.
18. What is your biggest strength and weakness?
19. Tell me about a piece of feedback you received that you did not like. What did you do about it?
20. Where do you see yourself in the next 2–3 years?

## E. Hiring Manager's Favorites (6)

21. Why do you want to change your current job?
22. Why should we hire you?
23. What has been your most challenging technical problem, and how did you solve it?
24. What kind of work environment or manager do you prefer?
25. How do you balance quality and speed in your work?
26. What do you know about our company and this role?
